Yes, under Regulation (EU) No 1177/2010, passengers may request compensation for a delay in arrival at the final destination as set out in the transport contract [sea-1177-2010, Article 19(1)].

The minimum compensation is 25% of the ticket price for delays of:
*   1 hour for scheduled journeys up to 4 hours;
*   2 hours for journeys between 4 and 8 hours;
*   3 hours for journeys between 8 and 24 hours;
*   6 hours for journeys over 24 hours [sea-1177-2010, Article 19(1)].

If the delay exceeds double these times, the compensation increases to 50% of the ticket price [sea-1177-2010, Article 1
